    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "How to use this workflow",
      "pos": [
        -4550,
        4890
      ],
      "size": [
        600,
        255
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 17,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Talking avatar on a body and background\n1. Set **Face portrait for FlashHead** to a clear image of the same person.\n2. Set the body source and **Background image**. The body source sets the final canvas size.\n3. FlashHead creates the voice-driven face; **Track face onto body + background** aligns it per frame.\n4. Set `region=face` for safer blending; try `head` when hair/head movement matters.\n5. Optional: connect a full-person MASK to avoid automatic person segmentation.\n6. The person video should show the same person, cover the whole audio, and be near 25 fps; its detected FPS is connected automatically."
      ]
    },
